  "result": "Season 1's full year of trips data shows half-day AM/PM trips catch essentially zero yellowtail all year, while overnight and 1.5-day trips have sharp shoulder-season spikes (best $/share by far), and 3/4-day trips are the solid cheap play in the spring/early-summer window. I rewrote `strategy.py` to stay PTO-free by only booking offers with empty `pto_dates` (which correctly covers Fri/Sat-departure overnight and Fri-departure 1.5-day trips per the rules' own examples) and to pick whichever eligible class currently shows real yellowtail in the last 14-60 days of pooled trip data, rather than hardcoding season-1's specific hot months since season 2 replays a different year.\n\nSummary: updated `strategy.py` (data-driven, zero-PTO, class-agnostic booking rule) and `notes.md` (season-1 catch-rate-by-class/month analysis and what to watch); no forum post made this turn to keep the edge.",
